# Trivy ignore file — documented suppressions (ISO 27001 A.8.8 / T10)
#
# The convoyplan-updater image is built FROM docker:cli and bundles the
# docker-buildx and docker-compose CLI plugins. The vulnerabilities below live
# in those upstream-bundled plugin binaries (vendored containerd / moby / Go),
# not in our code, and cannot be patched by us without a fixed upstream
# docker:cli release. The updater container only runs our own trusted update
# scripts (git pull + `docker compose pull/up`); it does not parse untrusted
# MIME input, expose the moby authorization plugin API, or rely on
# runAsNonRoot — so none of these are exploitable here (VEX: not_affected).
#
# Re-evaluate once a patched docker:cli base image is available and drop the
# entries the bump resolves. Review by: 2026-09-10.

# containerd user ID handling bypass allows runAsNonRoot evasion.
# Bundled in docker-buildx/compose; the updater does not use runAsNonRoot.
# Fixed upstream in containerd 2.2.4.
CVE-2026-46680

# containerd v2 CVEs affecting docker-buildx (v2.2.4) and docker-compose
# (v2.2.3) CLI plugins bundled in docker:cli. All three are fixed upstream in
# containerd 2.2.5 / 2.1.9; a docker:cli release picking up those versions
# will resolve them. The updater container only runs our own trusted update
# scripts and does not expose any containerd API surface (VEX: not_affected).
# Re-evaluate when a patched docker:cli image is released. Review by: 2026-09-21.
CVE-2026-53488
CVE-2026-53489
CVE-2026-53492

# Moby authorization bypass. Bundled docker engine libs; the updater image
# ships only the docker CLI — no dockerd / authz plugin endpoint is exposed.
# Fixed upstream in docker/moby 29.3.1.
CVE-2026-34040

# Go stdlib MIME header DoS (net/textproto). The updater parses no untrusted
# MIME input. Fixed upstream in Go 1.25.11 / 1.26.4.
CVE-2026-42504

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# convoyplan-graphhopper: vulnerabilities bundled inside the upstream
# graphhopper-web JAR (graphhopper/Dockerfile, GH_VERSION pin). We cannot patch
# individual libraries inside the upstream fat JAR; fixing them requires a
# GraphHopper release that bumps these dependencies (evaluate a GH_VERSION
# upgrade — note that major bumps can change the graph format and force a
# re-import on every instance).
#
# Exposure assessment (VEX: not_affected): the GraphHopper container is only
# reachable inside the Docker network and on 127.0.0.1 (docker-compose.yml);
# the sole client is our backend sending well-formed routing requests. It never
# receives untrusted external traffic. The remaining input is the OSM PBF
# extract, downloaded over HTTPS from the operator-configured Geofabrik URL —
# worst case for the parser CVEs below is a DoS of the one-time graph import.
# Review by: 2026-09-10.

# jackson-core: StackoverflowError on deeply nested input. GraphHopper only
# parses its own config and our backend's requests. Fixed in jackson 2.15.0.
CVE-2025-52999

# protobuf-java: DoS in binary/textformat parsing. Used for OSM PBF import
# (trusted, operator-configured Geofabrik source); worst case import DoS.
CVE-2021-22569
CVE-2022-3509
CVE-2022-3510
CVE-2024-7254

# commons-io XmlStreamReader DoS on untrusted input — no untrusted XML reaches
# GraphHopper. Fixed in commons-io 2.14.0.
CVE-2024-47554

# Jetty HTTP request smuggling / gzip buffer corruption. Jetty serves only
# internal Docker-network requests from our backend — no untrusted clients,
# no intermediary proxy chain to smuggle through.
CVE-2026-2332
CVE-2024-13009

# SnakeYAML Constructor deserialization RCE. GraphHopper parses only its own
# baked-in config.yml (trusted, ships in our image) — no untrusted YAML input.
CVE-2022-1471

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# convoyplan-frontend: undici bundled inside Node.js 26 (node:26-alpine base
# image). undici is Node.js's built-in HTTP client (used by the native fetch()
# API) and cannot be updated independently of Node.js itself. A patched version
# is available in undici 6.27.0 / 7.28.0 / 8.5.0 — will be included in a
# future node:26-alpine image. Review by: 2026-09-21.
#
# CVE-2026-12151: undici 6.26.0 — unbounded memory growth via WebSocket client
# (DoS). The frontend container runs the SvelteKit Node.js SSR server, which
# serves HTTP responses and never initiates outgoing WebSocket connections via
# undici (VEX: not_affected).
CVE-2026-12151
